**Read:** [GeMS — Geologic Map Schema — USGS](../sources/GeMS-Map-Schema.lingua#r_6JP32YH79HZAV8JYYKVV1WER0J), the complete specification; [Levantamento da geodiversidade — SGB technical guide, volume 5 version 4](../sources/SGB-Geodiversity-Methods.lingua#r_7QW5KYAYK9SB2MT3R6MNCFAQWK), the complete guide; [QGIS Training Manual — QGIS project](../sources/QGIS-Training-Manual.lingua#r_65XJEHNY3P1ESW5KF5V0871SFQ), the full basic/vector/raster/layout/projection/analysis training sequence and relevant processing logs; [Digital Cartographic Standard for Geologic Map Symbolization — FGDC/USGS](../sources/Geologic-Map-Symbolization.lingua#r_7DHXSTN5K3KF1EPTPG18RM5K1K), all conventions used in the original map.

A geological publication should preserve observation locations, methods, map units, contacts, orientations, sections, source references, and the distinction between measured and interpreted elements. Coordinates and persistent observation/sample identities connect these parts. A visually complete layout cannot compensate for missing provenance or contradictory unit relations.

Study GeMS as a specification for representing geological maps, not as proof that a dataset is geologically correct. Compare its observations, descriptions, map units, confidence, and references with the chosen regional method. Schema validation and substantive geological review answer different questions.

Use GIS with explicit coordinate systems, transformations, scale, source dates, processing steps, and versions. Record original observations separately from edits and derived geometry. A later revised interpretation should remain connected to the evidence and the earlier explanation rather than overwriting their identity.

**Work:** complete the QGIS training modules and publish an original small interpretive map/section in your own study workspace. Include a readable legend, evidence/source account, coordinate reference, scale, observed/inferred distinctions, and uncertainty. Reopen it in a fresh workspace and independently check selected coordinates, orientations, contacts, and unit relationships. Compare its content with the full GeMS specification and SGB guide, explaining differences in purpose.

Keep original field data and licensed external source maps distinct. The Lince trail only references these studies and sources through ordinary Records; it does not require a new map importer, a publication manifest, or a bundled GIS/data service.

**Continue:** [Test a geological interpretation beyond goodness of fit](Geological-models-uncertainty-and-independent-tests.lingua#r_5CM8MEVHEFDCX3H9YZ0S60FRPR).

**Return:** [Geology — Earth materials, processes, history, and investigation](../Geology.lingua#r_3CK43VQS79NK0STWNPSCS8YM06).
